---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Quiz from '../../../../components/Quiz.astro';

const lang = 'en';
---

<Layout 
  title="Required Documents for Marriage in Denmark | Express Boda"
  description="Clear and minimal document checklist for international couples to get married in Denmark. No birth certificates required for most. Free document check."
  lang={lang}
  noindex={true}
  alternateLanguages={[]}
>

  <!-- HERO SECTION -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-100 to-[#FAFAFC] pt-14 pb-12 px-6 border-b border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center space-y-6">
      
      <!-- Badge -->
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-full text-blue-700 text-xs font-semibold">
        <span>📋 Simple & Transparent Requirements</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-slate-900">
        What Documents Do You Need to Get Married in Denmark?
      </h1>

      <p class="text-slate-600 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Unlike traditional bureaucratic marriages, Denmark requires a minimal, straightforward set of documents. In most cases, you don't even need birth certificates or complex legalizations.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="#checklist" class="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition shadow-md text-base block">
          View Document Checklist ↓
        </a>
        <a href="/en/#checker" class="bg-white hover:bg-slate-50 text-slate-800 border border-slate-300 font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition shadow-sm text-base block">
          Check via 1-min Quiz ⚡
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CORE CHECKLIST SECTION -->
  <section id="checklist" class="py-16 px-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Standard Document Checklist</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600">The core paperwork required by the Danish Agency of Family Law (AFL) for international couples</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      
      <!-- Doc 1: Passports -->
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-bold mb-4">🛂</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-2">Valid Passports</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Scans of the main pages of valid passports for both partners. 
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Must be valid for at least 3 months past your travel date</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> All corners and text must be fully visible in scans</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Doc 2: Legal Residence -->
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600 flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-bold mb-4">🇪🇺</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-2">Legal Residence Proof</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Proof of legal entry or residency in your current country of residence or the EU (e.g., residence permit, visa, or Schengen entry stamp).
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Residence cards (TIE, Blue Card, etc.) or valid visas</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Flight tickets or entry stamps if traveling for the wedding</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Doc 3: Marital Status -->
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-bold mb-4">📜</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-2">Certificate of Marital Status</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
            A document proving your current civil status (single, divorced, or widowed). 
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Certificate of Singleness / Civil Status Extract</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Must be recent (typically issued within the last 3–4 months)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Doc 4: Previous Marriages -->
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-bold mb-4">⚖️</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-2">Divorce or Death Certificates</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Required only if one or both partners have been previously married.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Final divorce decree with official stamp/dissolution date</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>✓</span> Death certificate of former spouse if widowed</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SITUATION BREAKDOWN (EU vs Non-EU) -->
  <section class="bg-slate-50 py-16 px-6 border-t border-b border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Requirements by Your Residency Status</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Depending on where you live and your citizenship, small nuances may apply</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-blue-600 font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">EU / EEA Citizens</div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-lg mb-2">Living in EU</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The simplest case. Usually requires valid passports, a certificate of marital status from your home municipality or consulate, and proof of residence.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Third-Country Citizens</div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-lg mb-2">With EU Residence Permit</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            If you hold a valid European residence card (e.g., in Spain, Germany, etc.), you can easily marry in Denmark. We ensure all residency permits align with AFL guidelines.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Tourist / Visa Entry</div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-lg mb-2">Binational Couples</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Even if one partner enters on a Schengen visa or visa-free, marriage in Denmark is fully legal. We audit entry stamps and dates to guarantee compliance.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FREE CHECK BANNER / CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
    <div class="bg-blue-900 text-white p-10 rounded-3xl shadow-xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold">Not sure if your documents are sufficient?</h2>
      <p class="text-blue-100 text-base max-w-xl mx-auto">
        Don't risk rejections or delays with the Danish Agency of Family Law. Let our experts review your papers for free before submission.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <a href="/en/#checker" class="inline-block bg-white text-blue-900 hover:bg-blue-50 font-bold px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition shadow-md text-base">
          Start Free Document Check →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ FOR DOCUMENTS -->
  <section class="bg-slate-50 py-16 px-6 border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-10">Frequently Asked Questions About Documents</h2>
      
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 p-6 cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center select-none">
            Do documents need to be translated into Danish?
            <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180 text-blue-600 font-normal">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-slate-600 text-sm border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <p>No! The Danish Agency of Family Law (AFL) officially accepts documents in <strong>English, German, and Danish</strong>. In most cases, standard international documents or English versions do not require any translation.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 p-6 cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center select-none">
            Are birth certificates required?
            <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180 text-blue-600 font-normal">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-slate-600 text-sm border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <p>In the vast majority of cases, <strong>birth certificates are not required</strong> by the Danish authorities. This is one of the main reasons why getting married in Denmark is significantly faster and easier than in other countries.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 p-6 cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center select-none">
            How old can my Certificate of Marital Status be?
            <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180 text-blue-600 font-normal">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-slate-600 text-sm border-t border-slate-100 pt-4">
            <p>The certificate proving your civil status must be fresh — typically issued within the last <strong>3 to 4 months</strong> prior to your application submission date to ensure it reflects your current status accurately.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
